1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,369
Gye Su-jeong? Are you Gye Su-jeong?

3
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,873
Who are you?

4
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:25,251
The miracle worker? Doctor X?

5
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:47,065
We need your help at my village,
Gye Su-jeong.

6
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:48,817
My little sister was shot.

7
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:52,529
Is that why you're here?

8
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:56,074
You came to find me? All by yourself?

9
00:01:57,408 --> 00:02:00,537
Her only hope is Gye Su-jeong.
That's what he said.

10
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,082
Who said that? Someone in your village?

11
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:05,500
Baba.

12
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:09,671
- Baba?
- Uh-huh. He's a doctor like you.

13
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:13,633
Baba's hurt too, but he told me
my little sister has a bullet in her head,

14
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:15,635
and only you can save her.

15
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:20,515
Gye Su-jeong, please help us.

16
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:47,375
Okay. Let's go.

17
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:06,019
What's this?

18
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:16,654
There's lots of soldiers everywhere.

19
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:18,573
I'll just be in the way.

20
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:21,451
Look. That's my village.
It shows you how to get to it.

21
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:25,371
Uh-uh. Your foot's hurt.
You need treatment.

22
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:27,582
I'm gonna take you with me.

23
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:29,292
Well, then… here.

24
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:32,295
What?

25
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:34,422
Why?

26
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:36,591
If the soldiers try to shoot you
in the back.

27
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:41,763
You need to stay alive
so you can save my sister's life.

28
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:57,987
What happens if the soldiers
try to shoot me here?

29
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:00,490
Hmm.

30
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:22,512
What's your name?

31
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,639
Baraka.

32
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:27,558
Oh, "Blessings."

33
00:04:30,019 --> 00:04:31,104
What's your sister's name?

34
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:32,730
Neema.

35
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:36,234
With "Blessings" and "Grace,"

36
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:40,113
I'm sure that everyone
is going to be okay.

37
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:44,033
Close your eyes now.

38
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,502
I want you to keep your eyes closed

39
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:56,796
'til I tell you to open them up.

40
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:57,880
Hmm?

41
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:02,176
And when you open your eyes,
your sister will be there.

42
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,761
Keep them closed, okay?

43
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:07,390
All right.

44
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,518
Make sure to hold on tight.

45
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,526
All right, it's time to go.

46
00:05:26,617 --> 00:05:29,495
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

47
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:39,047
<i>This just in.</i>

48
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,841
<i>We have had reports saying that</i>
<i>former President Ji Du-seok</i>

49
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:44,677
<i>was found unconscious</i>
<i>and is being rushed to the hospital.</i>

50
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:48,389
<i>We now turn to our reporter</i>
<i>at the scene for more details.</i>

51
00:05:56,856 --> 00:06:00,735
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

52
00:06:07,825 --> 00:06:09,660
Mr. Oh Sang-beom, is he okay?

53
00:06:10,995 --> 00:06:12,080
Did you find him?

54
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:13,998
Well, did you?

55
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:18,002
Hey, I can stay longer.
Please let me help.

56
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,922
What do we need an intern
hanging around for? After all, I'm here.

57
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:25,802
VIP 06
OH SANG-BEOM

58
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,973
One of those security officers
came by earlier

59
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:33,810
and said he'll need to be moved
into a different room soon.

60
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:35,895
They want us to move him? Why?

61
00:06:35,978 --> 00:06:38,356
He said they need to empty
the whole floor out,

62
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,233
and they'll find him another room.

63
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:43,903
They come out to greet him and fawn
over him like they'd do anything for him,

64
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,738
then they pull this crap? Unbelievable.

65
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:53,204
Let's just go. She's not going anywhere
right now, no matter who comes.

66
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:56,249
- Let's get out of here.
- Damn it.

67
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,555
Director Bu is going to hear about this.

68
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,181
Director Bu probably gave the order.

69
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:14,475
So then, we tell him
it's the wrong thing to do.

70
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,728
The hospital made a commitment
to take care of him.

71
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:20,106
He didn't choose this.
We brought him all the way out here.

72
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,899
Yeah, but…

73
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,609
Staying here would be weird.

74
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:27,071
Yeah.

75
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:29,615
Although, this whole thing
is pretty weird.

76
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:31,284
- Huh?
- I mean, come on.

77
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:32,952
Does this make sense to you guys?

78
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,085
WE CONDEMN JI DU-SEOK, A BLIGHT ON HISTORY

79
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:43,212
HOPE DAILY

80
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:48,050
JI DU-SEOK, APOLOGIZE TO THE PEOPLE!

81
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:49,385
BRING DOWN JI DU-SEOK

82
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:11,908
A WEEK AGO

83
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:39,310
- Welcome!
- Welcome!

84
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:42,813
Welcome.

85
00:08:51,405 --> 00:08:52,823
Good to see you.

86
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:06,879
So, what brings you
all the way out here so suddenly?

87
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:08,839
If we'd have known in advance
that you were coming, we'd--

88
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:11,050
We wanted to surprise you.

89
00:09:11,133 --> 00:09:14,095
Oh! And what a surprise it was.
You definitely succeeded.

90
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:16,180
Director Bu seemed quite surprised too.

91
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:21,143
Yes, well… I was curious as to what
brought you here without any notice.

92
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,770
Where should we begin?

93
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:27,483
Oh, uh, it'd be our pleasure
to talk them over with you.

94
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,568
Oh, that reminds me.

95
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:32,238
At the Magnolia meeting,
you brought up a proposal regarding

96
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:35,116
planning a task force
for normalizing hospital management--

97
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:36,200
There's a surgery we need you to do.

98
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:40,413
Pardon? Surgery? So… what surgery?

99
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:46,627
Why don't you have their doctor
write a patient referral--

100
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,504
If we could go through
the proper channels,

101
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,506
do you think that
he would've had to come here?

102
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:52,925
I'm not sure what you're saying.

103
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:55,720
- Could you be more specific about--
- We want a bullet taken out.

104
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:05,813
VICTIMS STILL OVERLOOKED AS SUPPORT STALLS
46 YEARS AFTER GWANGJU DEMOCRATIC UPRISING

105
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:12,153
Out of here.

106
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:15,990
Huh?

107
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:24,832
Oh Sang-beom, a 57-year-old male,
suffered a traumatic brain injury in 1980.

108
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:27,793
A bullet fragment was lodged in his head,
and he fell into a coma,

109
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:30,212
regaining consciousness 15 days later.

110
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:31,714
And now we'll view the site of the injury.

111
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:33,382
CASE 1: OH SANG-BEOM, M/57

112
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:35,509
Given the surgical techniques
and equipment at the time,

113
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:38,763
there was no guarantee he'd survive
an attempt to remove the fragment,

114
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:40,640
so it was left in place.

115
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:41,766
Due to the fragment's location,

116
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:45,978
he's still experiencing spasms on the left
side of his face, left arm, and left leg.

117
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:49,732
He also suffers from seizures, headaches,
and visual and auditory hallucinations

118
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:51,609
due to post-traumatic stress.

119
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:53,903
<i>After that incident,</i>

120
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,696
there was a fire at the hospital
where he was treated.

121
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,531
All of his medical records were lost.

122
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,659
So the fragment's exact location
is unknown.

123
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:02,953
- Can't we just run tests again?
- He said no.

124
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:06,624
He won't accept any treatment, either.
He just takes tons of painkillers.

125
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:09,293
Apparently, his older brother,
who was with him at the time,

126
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:13,381
used his body as a shield, took a bullet
for him, and he died at the scene.

127
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:15,633
Now he's got that, you know,
survivor's guilt.

128
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:18,427
And he keeps saying that
he just wants to live with it.

129
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:22,765
The point is, the gunfire
came from a helicopter.

130
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:25,434
You heard about that, right?

131
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:28,771
This guy and his brother
didn't just get shot with a plain old gun.

132
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,690
They got shot by an attack helicopter.

133
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:32,900
The martial law troops never admitted

134
00:11:32,983 --> 00:11:35,152
to any of the violent acts
they committed back then.

135
00:11:35,236 --> 00:11:36,987
But the proof of what they did…

136
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:39,990
is embedded inside his head.

137
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,744
Uh, but he refused to even get tested,
or even get treatment, right?

138
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:46,080
Well, that's why you need
to convince him to do it.

139
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:49,583
And if we promise to give government
support to him and all the victims,

140
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:52,420
we'll come off looking
like paragons of righteousness.

141
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:55,423
This is our chance to show
the power of white-coat solidarity.

142
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:58,300
- Our what?
- You know that med school quota issue?

143
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:01,178
This could help steer that
in our favor as well.

144
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:03,514
It'll boost the public's image
of doctors, too.

145
00:12:03,597 --> 00:12:07,393
Man, actually, if I could do it,
it'd be awesome publicity, you know?

146
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:08,853
- Oh, jeez.
- I'd do the surgery

147
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:11,272
and whip out the bullet
in front of people like, "Ta-da!" So cool.

148
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:12,732
That would've been amazing!

149
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:14,734
Damn, why didn't you specialize
in General Surgery?

150
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:16,277
- I know, right?
- Why our hospital?

151
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:19,447
Why do that surgery here?

152
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:23,701
Actually, no one else will do it.
We did ask around.

153
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:24,952
Well, we won't be doing it.

154
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,954
This was Magnolia's decision.

155
00:12:27,037 --> 00:12:28,873
Are you telling me
to blindly follow a decision

156
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,125
that could potentially endanger
this hospital?

157
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:36,797
You know this rotten view would be…
better higher up.

158
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:40,509
Ever wonder why the director's office
isn't on a higher floor?

159
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:48,476
You've never opened this door, have you?

160
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:50,728
It leads directly to the parking lot.

161
00:12:51,729 --> 00:12:54,440
As a director, you might find
you need a back door one day.

162
00:12:54,523 --> 00:12:58,027
A lower floor lacks authority,
a higher one has no back door,

163
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:59,945
so your office was put here.

164
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:02,323
To ensure a way out would always be there.

165
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:07,161
You think you'll never have to use
this door, don't you?

166
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:13,834
Huh? What? Just-- Just a moment.

167
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:16,587
I'm sorry to interrupt,
but this matter is urgent.

168
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:20,174
Director, a journalist
keeps calling us with questions.

169
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:26,180
He's asking if there's
any truth to the rumor

170
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:28,557
that the hospital is considering closing

171
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:32,061
due to their inability to cover
their accumulated debt.

172
00:13:34,021 --> 00:13:38,859
Director, the journalist mentioned
the exact amount of the deficit.

173
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:41,111
We need to stop the article
from being published.

174
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,496
You want us to take the fall.

175
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:52,456
What nonsense is this?

176
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:54,124
I mean, it's ridiculous.

177
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:57,753
Well, am I wrong?

178
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:03,217
Director, did you really think
we wouldn't know? We all know.

179
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,845
Listen. We're talking
about saving a life here.

180
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,972
Why are you so resistant to doing that?

181
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,600
It's quite amusing, isn't it?

182
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:15,271
That, out of all people,
we're hearing this from you, Doctor.

183
00:14:15,354 --> 00:14:16,480
Meaning what?

184
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:19,358
Stay out of this.
It's a neurosurgery issue.

185
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:22,236
Dr. Jang, please… That's enough.

186
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:24,280
Oh, really? So…

187
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:27,533
now you're a neurosurgeon
as well, are you?

188
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:29,326
Did you learn it from watching
Bae Heung-gon?

189
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,538
- You can't even open a skull, you idiot.
- What?

190
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,124
You can't just say whatever you want.
You hear me?

191
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:37,751
It'll be a table death
or a vegetative state. All right?

192
00:14:37,835 --> 00:14:41,088
So, basically, you're asking for us
to perform a surgery

193
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:43,549
with no guarantee the patient
will come out of the OR in one piece.

194
00:14:43,632 --> 00:14:45,509
We haven't even done
a proper examination yet.

195
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:47,887
You can't diagnose a patient
without a brain scan, can you?

196
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:52,057
Every single person in this country
is going to be watching us like a hawk

197
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,767
in case the patient dies on us.

198
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:55,853
Why would anyone do this?

199
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,271
Who's gonna do it?

200
00:14:57,354 --> 00:15:01,191
Are you gonna do it? Huh?
Who is going to do it?

201
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:05,487
Me! Me, me.

202
00:15:11,368 --> 00:15:12,411
I'll perform the surgery.

203
00:15:15,372 --> 00:15:17,499
Dr. Gye Su-jeong will jump at it.

204
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:21,253
- What?
- If we toss the bait, she'll take it.

205
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:24,673
Neither Dr. Gye Su-jeong nor
Ms. Jang Hui-suk will be able to resist.

206
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:26,967
I-If she fails though…

207
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:29,511
The consequences won't be borne by us.

208
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:32,181
They'll rest on shoulders
of Dr. Gye and Ms. Jang.

209
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:35,684
We could fire Dr. Gye Su-jeong,

210
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:38,729
and our hospital will be rid of her,
once and for all.

211
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:43,692
If she fails, Magnolia will never
let it go and our reputation would…

212
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:47,446
We won't be the only ones who go down.

213
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,782
He said, "White-coat solidarity."

214
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:51,659
If we go down,

215
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,078
we all go down together.

216
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:25,818
Given that we're doing the surgery,
and convincing the patient,

217
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:28,028
that looks a little light, you know?

218
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:30,781
There'll be another one,
once this whole thing is finished.

219
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,157
Oh, understood.

220
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:34,994
Oh, don't forget your…

221
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,205
I'm gonna leave it with you.

222
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:40,374
I'll get it later, with the rest of it.

223
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,167
I've got a lot of stuff.
I went shopping today.

224
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:44,169
See you soon, bye now.

225
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:56,015
"No possibility of failure,"
is that what she's saying?

226
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:14,116
So then, right in the middle
of the grocery store,

227
00:17:14,199 --> 00:17:16,827
I get a call demanding
I come over to see him.

228
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:19,705
I sit down and there's
a bag of money just sitting there.

229
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:22,416
How do I respond to that?
What am I supposed to do?

230
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:26,628
What else can I do? Just do it!

231
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:31,300
Hey, I didn't expect him
to call me back this soon.

232
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:35,763
Man, I was trying to play it so cool,
I didn't even ask how much was it was.

233
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:37,431
Let's figure it out.

234
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:41,268
How deep was the bag… Let me see. Okay.

235
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:43,312
A 50,000-won bill

236
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:46,315
is around… so that should be…

237
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:48,025
Hmm, roughly about…

238
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:51,987
Wow. Looks like we can…

239
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,531
Ah, come on. Would you just tell us
how much already?

240
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:58,035
- How much? How much? How much?
- It's a lot.

241
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:02,247
Enough for a new car!

242
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:06,251
- So cool!
- Thank you, God. Thank you, Buddha.

243
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:07,586
Thank you, thank you, thank you!

244
00:18:07,669 --> 00:18:10,339
Hey, if we get to live even one more day,
it's all thanks to you, Su-jeong.

245
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:12,925
Oh, totally,
that car was gonna kill us all.

246
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:14,384
I prayed every time I got in it.

247
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,804
I know, lately, we've been pushing it
more than driving it.

248
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:19,223
- Yeah, totally.
- Let's look up some car models.

249
00:18:19,306 --> 00:18:22,684
We clean up their mess,
and they scapegoat us.

250
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:27,815
He knew what he was doing.
He had all those witnesses.

251
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:32,444
He wanted them to see you volunteer,
so they could have someone to blame.

252
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:36,448
I knew all that when I texted you.

253
00:18:39,034 --> 00:18:40,994
Sick of being back in General Surgery yet?

254
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:45,165
Nothing but appendectomies all week long.

255
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,584
About that, don't call me anymore.

256
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:50,838
I've been doing appendectomies
all week too, thanks to you.

257
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:54,133
What's more,
you finish your surgeries way too fast.

258
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:56,176
Which means more surgeries,
so I keep getting busier.

259
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:01,682
What?

260
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:05,227
- It'll give you some energy.
- I've got my own, thanks.

261
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:09,940
Hey, why don't you just do surgeries

262
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:13,527
at the same speed as everyone else,
so I get a chance to catch my breath?

263
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:14,862
Seriously, it's a real drag.

264
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:16,780
<i>Run over to the conference hall right now.</i>

265
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:19,700
<i>- Say you'll do it, no matter what.</i>
- <i>Do what?</i>

266
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:26,290
Oh, what--

267
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:31,503
<i>Bullet, brain, surgery.</i>

268
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:36,300
<i>Train 114 is boarding</i>
<i>and will be departing from Platform 8.</i>

269
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,052
Here. Have some more. Enjoy.

270
00:19:39,136 --> 00:19:40,888
- Mmm.
- This too.

271
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:45,851
Oh!

272
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:47,060
Over here.

273
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:49,646
- Oh! Our little doctor.
- Hello.

274
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:53,775
I'm so happy that the hospital sent you
to accompany us, what a delight!

275
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:56,486
I haven't taken a train
anywhere in a while,

276
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:58,488
so actually, I'm kind of excited.

277
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:01,200
So I did all my homework before I came.

278
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:04,953
I read everything the hospital gave me,
along with some stuff I found myself.

279
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,246
I read those too.

280
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:07,873
Oh, right, of course.

281
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:09,041
I just brought them…

282
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:10,876
She'll look them over again on the train.

283
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,586
- Here, have this.
- Thanks so much.

284
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:17,216
Oh! Dr. Jo, over here! Over here!

285
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:18,467
Oh, come in!

286
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:21,261
- You're here!
- Hello.

287
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:24,890
Hey, why are you acting so shy?
We're all friends here, aren't we?

288
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:26,642
- Please join us.
- Thanks.

289
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:30,229
Well, I'm not sure why you need me to come
with you, but I will, since you asked.

290
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:33,857
Well, our plans for the company dinner
were ruined by that horrible person.

291
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:35,734
I was very disappointed.

292
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:38,362
And when you so kindly agreed
to help us with this,

293
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:40,322
I decided we should all go together.

294
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:42,407
Okay, but I'm an anesthesiologist.

295
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:46,078
Okay, look. See that naive simpleton

296
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:47,955
and that moody glutton?

297
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:50,415
Would you trust those two
to do your surgery?

298
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:53,293
We need someone there
who looks like a real doctor. That's you.

299
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:54,753
So you should just play along.

300
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:05,514
- Here, have some.
- Okay.

301
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,600
Looks like this place is about to close.

302
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:11,061
Yeah, so is my wallet.

303
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:13,689
I'll foot the bill just for today.

304
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:17,150
You know Dr. Gye pretty well now,
don't you?

305
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:19,903
- You're friends, right?
- Well, I wouldn't call us friends.

306
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,573
Oh, right.

307
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:25,617
Okay. It's gonna be a pretty long trip,

308
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:28,912
so before we go,
let's have a little pick-me-up.

309
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,330
Okay, okay.

310
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,333
- Here, have one.
- Oh, all right. Thank you very much.

311
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:37,671
Mmm.

312
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:40,215
Pretty good.

313
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:41,925
Mmm.

314
00:21:49,182 --> 00:21:50,183
I'm perking up.

315
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:55,314
Um, are you guys getting
the same text messages as me?

316
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,190
<i>Where are you? The train?</i>
<i>Are you eating? Is it good?</i>

317
00:21:57,274 --> 00:21:58,400
<i>What's Gwangju's specialty?</i>

318
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:00,235
<i>Hey, have you thought about me?</i>
<i>Are you at the station?</i>

319
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:02,446
<i>Bring a present. I'll call you</i>
<i>Fun Won-jin, and not Dull Won-jin.</i>

320
00:22:02,529 --> 00:22:03,989
<i>- Okay? You mad? You mad?</i>
- Oh, it's Dr. Kim?

321
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:06,158
<i>Please, Lady Macbeth,</i>
<i>answer me. I'm hurt. Hmph.</i>

322
00:22:06,241 --> 00:22:09,369
My phone is vibrating so much,
it's like my table's ready. I got this.

323
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:13,081
<i>Things must be slow in the ER.</i>

324
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:15,125
Oh, that's cruel.

325
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:18,337
Oh, Dr. Jo, that's a little harsh,
don't you think?

326
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:22,883
Jeez. The guy has no friends I guess.

327
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:26,553
What?

328
00:22:28,555 --> 00:22:29,598
That one's mine.

329
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,643
I have tons of friends.

330
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:34,978
We always hang out together.

331
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:38,065
Huh. What about you two?

332
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:40,025
What are you talking about?
I've got lots of friends.

333
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:41,943
- You have no friends.
- No, I've got a bunch of 'em.

334
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:43,904
- Name one, then.
- Wait--

335
00:22:43,987 --> 00:22:46,448
Three, two, one. You don't have any.

336
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:03,006
<i>At that time,</i>
<i>I was running a tiny shoe store.</i>

337
00:23:04,257 --> 00:23:07,135
<i>May was an exciting month for us,</i>

338
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:11,848
<i>because we celebrated Children's Day,</i>
<i>Parents' Day, and Teachers' Day.</i>

339
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:13,809
<i>But now…</i>

340
00:23:27,948 --> 00:23:29,449
GWANGJU, 1980

341
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:30,534
- Have a nice day.
- Thank you.

342
00:23:30,617 --> 00:23:32,702
Okay, I'll show you some of my shoes,

343
00:23:33,286 --> 00:23:35,872
but I'm gonna need
to see your money first.

344
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:37,499
Have you got money with you?

345
00:23:38,208 --> 00:23:39,543
First, show me the shoes.

346
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:42,504
The nerve of this kid, just unbelievable.

347
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:44,256
You're Seung-beom's little brother, right?

348
00:23:44,339 --> 00:23:46,633
He shines shoes in front
of the government office, doesn't he?

349
00:23:46,716 --> 00:23:49,219
Oh, wow! You knew that?

350
00:23:49,302 --> 00:23:51,471
Um, well, if you know who we are,
I guess we're pretty famous.

351
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,932
Oh, you must be joking.

352
00:23:54,724 --> 00:23:58,145
What do you mean, famous?
You sure don't look like you're famous.

353
00:23:58,228 --> 00:24:01,022
My goodness, what a riot.

354
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:04,860
Anyway you've been hanging around in front
of my shop for the past few days now.

355
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:06,611
Were you looking at those shoes out there?

356
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,738
What a spoiled brat you are.

357
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:11,158
Your brother works hard
to support your mother and you,

358
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:13,910
shining people's shoes out there,
day and night.

359
00:24:13,994 --> 00:24:17,831
And you come into my store here, looking
to buy shoes with the money he made?

360
00:24:17,914 --> 00:24:18,915
No, with my money.

361
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:20,125
Your own money?

362
00:24:21,168 --> 00:24:23,170
I guess I owe you an apology, kiddo.

363
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:26,506
I've been saving up
to buy my brother some shoes.

364
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:30,385
Gracious.

365
00:24:32,679 --> 00:24:34,473
You two are a lot alike, aren't you?

366
00:24:35,056 --> 00:24:38,268
Seems like you're just as kind
and hard-working as your brother.

367
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:40,854
Ah! Do you really mean it?

368
00:24:41,771 --> 00:24:44,524
We're not related, actually.

369
00:24:45,442 --> 00:24:47,277
Uh, when I was four,

370
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:51,031
my birth mom and I rented a room from Mom.

371
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:53,074
But she ran away and left me there.

372
00:24:53,992 --> 00:24:56,703
And Mom and Seung-beom
have been my family since then.

373
00:24:57,454 --> 00:25:01,374
And I'm the real reason
my brother always has to work so hard.

374
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:04,628
He'd only have to work half as much
if it weren't for me.

375
00:25:04,711 --> 00:25:06,630
Nah, it's not just because of you, kid.

376
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:10,926
Hold on a second. Be right back.

377
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:15,847
Oh, um, my brother, uh,
he likes classical music.

378
00:25:16,431 --> 00:25:18,350
Also, my brother he's…

379
00:25:19,684 --> 00:25:21,770
I know. Inelegant.

380
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:23,647
You mean "intelligent," "intelligent"!

381
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:27,609
If he were inelegant, that means
that he would be clumsy or impolite.

382
00:25:28,276 --> 00:25:31,363
Okay, but you know what I mean, right?

383
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:33,448
I mean he's really, really smart,
you know?

384
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:36,076
He wants to learn the piano one day.

385
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:37,786
For him, it'll probably be easy.

386
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:42,999
HANBAEK DRESS SHOES

387
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:44,793
Okay, let's see.

388
00:25:46,002 --> 00:25:47,337
Yeah, these are the ones.

389
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:49,005
Take a look.

390
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:51,091
- What do you think?
- Hmm.

391
00:25:55,929 --> 00:25:57,305
Yeah, they're great.

392
00:26:35,844 --> 00:26:36,845
Here.

393
00:26:37,971 --> 00:26:38,972
Take 'em.

394
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:40,557
Huh?

395
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,309
Um, no.

396
00:26:44,394 --> 00:26:47,147
You know, I just remembered.

397
00:26:47,230 --> 00:26:50,609
These shoes… look, look, look
at the laces. See the problem?

398
00:26:51,651 --> 00:26:53,278
If you look closely,

399
00:26:53,361 --> 00:26:56,323
the laces are a little uneven, right?

400
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:59,576
- I don't think so.
- You don't think so?

401
00:27:00,243 --> 00:27:03,747
Kid, you're smart, but I think
you need to get your eyes examined.

402
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,752
No one's gonna buy these. They're yours.

403
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:14,341
If you save up some more money,
right, then one day…

404
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:17,844
you can get a piano for your brother.

405
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:27,395
Hey, whoa, whoa, what are you doing? What?

406
00:27:27,479 --> 00:27:28,813
"I won't forget your kindness."

407
00:27:28,897 --> 00:27:30,899
Mom says, when I say that,
I should bow down.

408
00:27:30,982 --> 00:27:34,444
Jeez, for a minute there, I thought
you were asking for some New Year's money.

409
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:38,865
Hey, hold on a minute.
I'll get you some shoe polish too.

410
00:27:41,576 --> 00:27:44,287
- We've gotta run! Gotta run!
- Stop right there!

411
00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:45,872
They're coming for us!

412
00:27:45,955 --> 00:27:47,415
- They have guns!
- Run! They're using gas!

413
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:50,001
- Move! Move!
- What the hell's going on?

414
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,170
Come on!

415
00:27:52,253 --> 00:27:54,631
- We have to get out of here!
- Is there another protest?

416
00:27:54,714 --> 00:27:56,049
- Where are you?
- Hurry! Move!

417
00:27:56,132 --> 00:27:58,385
Are they coming
from the government building?

418
00:27:58,468 --> 00:28:01,012
Excuse me!

419
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:03,098
Don't go! Come here, come here, come here!

420
00:28:04,015 --> 00:28:05,809
My brother! I have to get him.

421
00:28:08,937 --> 00:28:10,855
- No, stay back.
- I have to get to him.

422
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:12,148
You can't do that!

423
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:14,651
But he could be hurt.

424
00:28:14,734 --> 00:28:16,903
Hey, let go. I said let go!

425
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:25,412
Don't go that way!
You'll run right into them!

426
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:26,788
This way! This way!

427
00:28:29,624 --> 00:28:30,667
Run!

428
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:32,877
Hurry! Hurry, hurry!

429
00:28:33,878 --> 00:28:34,879
No.

430
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:38,258
No.

431
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,241
Seung!

432
00:29:06,995 --> 00:29:09,080
Seung-beom! Where are you?

433
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,083
Seung!

434
00:29:24,387 --> 00:29:27,307
<i>That was "Qui a tué</i>
<i>grand' maman?" by Michel Polnareff.</i>

435
00:29:27,390 --> 00:29:28,767
Su-jeong.

436
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:33,646
<i>It is well-known to us citizens of Gwangju</i>
<i>as the original song behind "Song of May."</i>

437
00:29:34,647 --> 00:29:36,065
<i>When "Song of May" was banned,</i>

438
00:29:36,149 --> 00:29:40,195
<i>radio stations across the nation played</i>
<i>this song around May 18th to</i>

439
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:42,280
<i>- commemorate the victims of the massacre…</i>
- We're getting off at the next stop.

440
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:48,870
Well, at the very least, he has people
he can rely on taking care of him.

441
00:29:48,953 --> 00:29:52,123
They were in the hospital with him
back them, apparently. He's a doctor.

442
00:29:53,416 --> 00:29:55,835
So he's been going there
every day, really?

443
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:01,549
<i>It seems they were never able</i>
<i>to find his brother's body.</i>

444
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:04,886
<i>He still hasn't had a grave made for him.</i>

445
00:30:05,512 --> 00:30:08,181
<i>Evidently, there are a lot of people</i>
<i>from back then</i>

446
00:30:08,264 --> 00:30:09,724
<i>who were never found.</i>

447
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:11,810
<i>I guess that's why he goes there.</i>

448
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,815
<i>He shines shoes for a living</i>

449
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:21,444
<i>and after work, he goes there,</i>
<i>rain or shine.</i>

450
00:30:22,195 --> 00:30:25,156
<i>For over 40 years, almost his whole life.</i>

451
00:30:28,993 --> 00:30:30,745
<i>They said he doesn't talk.</i>

452
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:33,289
<i>At some point, he just stopped speaking.</i>

453
00:30:34,749 --> 00:30:36,668
<i>The last thing they heard him say was,</i>

454
00:30:36,751 --> 00:30:38,795
<i>"It's all my fault."</i>

455
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:42,090
<i>"I want to die because I'm alive."</i>

456
00:30:42,173 --> 00:30:47,554
<i>"But dying seems too easy, so I want</i>
<i>to pay for it by living in pain."</i>

457
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:25,216
WOO JAE-GYEONG INTERNAL MEDICINE

458
00:31:45,028 --> 00:31:46,029
Hello.

459
00:31:47,655 --> 00:31:49,407
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

460
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:50,700
Please come in.

461
00:31:55,538 --> 00:31:58,291
These folks here
were at the hospital back then, too.

462
00:31:58,374 --> 00:31:59,876
I thought we could talk together.

463
00:32:01,502 --> 00:32:02,837
Have a seat.

464
00:32:15,725 --> 00:32:18,394
So you're saying
she performed this surgery

465
00:32:18,478 --> 00:32:20,897
and will also be doing
Sang-beom's surgery?

466
00:32:20,980 --> 00:32:22,148
Yes, that's right.

467
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:25,985
All three of them
are truly exceptional doctors.

468
00:32:29,572 --> 00:32:33,701
That's extraordinary.
I've never seen anything like this before.

469
00:32:37,830 --> 00:32:40,625
Hey, say something, okay?

470
00:32:40,708 --> 00:32:43,503
Good God, they're telling you
the government's paying for your surgery.

471
00:32:43,586 --> 00:32:45,004
Hey, would you keep it down?

472
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:47,674
He can hear you just fine. Don't yell.

473
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:51,594
You'll end up like Geun-sik
if you don't take care of yourself.

474
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:54,722
Now why would you bring that up?

475
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:58,434
How many more of us
do we need to see end up like that?

476
00:32:59,477 --> 00:33:01,729
If we all just fade away, one by one,

477
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:04,524
then people are gonna forget about us!

478
00:33:04,607 --> 00:33:06,943
The slate gets wiped clean,
like it never happened at all.

479
00:33:07,026 --> 00:33:09,612
All right, that's enough now, seriously.

480
00:33:09,696 --> 00:33:10,863
Sang-beom.

481
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:13,116
You can do whatever you want. Okay?

482
00:33:13,199 --> 00:33:15,660
We shouldn't have come.
Let's go, Yeong-pyo.

483
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:19,247
Hey, listen,
it'll get really bad once we're all gone.

484
00:33:19,330 --> 00:33:21,791
It'd actually be better
if the slate was wiped clean.

485
00:33:21,874 --> 00:33:24,585
'Cause they'll keep saying
it was North Korea that did it,

486
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:27,255
or that we all died
because we were shooting at each other.

487
00:33:27,338 --> 00:33:30,341
Or that we were the ones that shot first
and killed the soldiers!

488
00:33:31,259 --> 00:33:34,053
That's what they're gonna write
on that slate.

489
00:33:34,887 --> 00:33:36,806
If we all disappear one by one,

490
00:33:37,557 --> 00:33:38,891
that'll happen for sure!

491
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:42,311
We need to stay alive.

492
00:33:43,354 --> 00:33:45,898
We need to stick around for a long time
and show them.

493
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,818
Right, Sang-beom? Right?

494
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:52,822
Come on, man! Say something!

495
00:33:54,073 --> 00:33:57,326
Oh, Nurse Jin, you came just in time.

496
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:59,704
Give everyone a bottle. Yeah.

497
00:33:59,787 --> 00:34:01,914
- Oh, for goodness' sake…
- Good idea.

498
00:34:01,998 --> 00:34:05,043
You should go outside
and cool off a bit. Go ahead.

499
00:34:06,419 --> 00:34:10,006
Hey, Beom, you know how he is, right?

500
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:12,759
Whenever Yeong-pyo has been drinking,

501
00:34:12,842 --> 00:34:17,263
he starts crying about how much
his heart breaks for you,

502
00:34:17,346 --> 00:34:20,308
and how it must've been
so terribly lonely for you

503
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:22,769
to live like that for all these years.

504
00:34:25,521 --> 00:34:26,731
The funny thing is, though…

505
00:34:27,690 --> 00:34:29,901
even though he's pushing 60 now,

506
00:34:31,527 --> 00:34:35,239
in our eyes, you're still 12 years old,

507
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:38,284
a boy who was crying his eyes out

508
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:41,079
and begging to go home.

509
00:34:42,497 --> 00:34:45,416
It didn't matter
if you were asleep or awake,

510
00:34:46,417 --> 00:34:49,170
you'd ask for your brother
and you'd ask for your mom.

511
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:51,255
Do you remember?

512
00:34:51,881 --> 00:34:53,633
You were sleeping and you woke up

513
00:34:53,716 --> 00:34:56,928
and you were sobbing
and saying, "It's too heavy."

514
00:34:57,011 --> 00:35:00,765
You'd say it over and over,
"It's too heavy. It's too heavy."

515
00:35:01,474 --> 00:35:04,227
I thought, "He must've been so frightened

516
00:35:04,310 --> 00:35:07,897
that he confused the word 'heavy'
with the word 'scary.'"

517
00:35:08,731 --> 00:35:10,358
My heart just broke for you.

518
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:19,617
As a doctor,

519
00:35:20,993 --> 00:35:23,663
I have some idea
of what kind of surgery this is.

520
00:35:23,746 --> 00:35:26,541
Isn't there a pretty high
probability of failure?

521
00:35:34,632 --> 00:35:35,758
Do you think that he'll…

522
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:38,261
actually make it?

523
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:41,055
Failure's a possibility.

524
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:45,059
If we fail, you will die.

525
00:35:47,270 --> 00:35:48,813
You don't have to have the surgery.

526
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:50,857
Right now, you might be uncomfortable,

527
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,317
but at least you're not dead, you know?

528
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:58,698
Oh, what she means is we respect
your choice and your opinion.

529
00:35:58,781 --> 00:36:00,533
Are you happy the way you are though?

530
00:36:01,409 --> 00:36:02,869
Living like this, barely existing?

531
00:36:08,291 --> 00:36:13,004
Just surviving life while trying to cope
with constant pain until you die?

532
00:36:14,338 --> 00:36:15,756
Is that what you really want to do?

533
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:26,309
This whole stack is nothing but…

534
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:29,103
painkiller prescriptions.

535
00:36:38,571 --> 00:36:40,573
You will die, meet your end eventually,

536
00:36:41,490 --> 00:36:43,034
so it's the same either way.

537
00:36:45,244 --> 00:36:48,164
If you do nothing
and keep living the way you are now,

538
00:36:48,247 --> 00:36:49,332
you don't have a prayer.

539
00:36:58,633 --> 00:37:01,802
Uh, like she said, it's up to you.

540
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:04,013
You don't have to do the operation.

541
00:37:04,513 --> 00:37:06,599
But why don't we just run some tests?

542
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:09,852
We can only know for sure
once we see the test results.

543
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:11,896
We can talk about the results,

544
00:37:11,979 --> 00:37:13,439
then you can leave if you want.

545
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:15,858
Just get the scans done, okay?

546
00:37:18,402 --> 00:37:19,445
Yeah.

547
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:53,271
Hey, why stop with the scans?

548
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:54,939
I mean, if you're going to Seoul,

549
00:37:55,022 --> 00:37:57,692
you should do lots of fine dining
and plenty of sightseeing.

550
00:37:58,484 --> 00:38:02,738
Sang-beom.
You deserve to do that, you really do.

551
00:38:26,887 --> 00:38:27,888
Well…

552
00:38:29,390 --> 00:38:32,935
It seems nobody else could bear
to see Sang-beom leaving.

553
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,855
So I'll be their representative.

554
00:38:35,938 --> 00:38:39,108
Once he arrives, he'll be admitted,
and then we'll start the imaging.

555
00:38:39,775 --> 00:38:40,776
We'll keep you updated.

556
00:38:43,863 --> 00:38:46,824
Please don't hesitate to contact me
if you ever feel anxious or worried.

557
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:49,327
- I'll be sure to answer.
- Ah.

558
00:38:49,410 --> 00:38:51,662
- This is <i>gimbap</i>. Huh?
- Oh!

559
00:38:52,538 --> 00:38:53,706
Oh.

560
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:56,751
Oh, wow.

561
00:38:58,419 --> 00:39:01,630
Hey, I'll head up there
on the day of the surgery.

562
00:39:01,714 --> 00:39:03,049
Looking forward to it.

563
00:39:04,759 --> 00:39:06,218
This is really good.

564
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:08,804
- Yeah?
- Oh.

565
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:11,223
Her surgical prowess
is as great as her appetite.

566
00:39:11,307 --> 00:39:12,725
Don't you worry.

567
00:39:12,808 --> 00:39:16,896
Oh, well, maybe I should've brought ten
more, then, or even a hundred more? Huh?

568
00:39:16,979 --> 00:39:18,731
Huh?

569
00:39:21,984 --> 00:39:24,987
We all chipped in a little.
This is for you.

570
00:39:25,571 --> 00:39:27,031
Hey, take it.

571
00:39:27,114 --> 00:39:28,491
Just take it, really.

572
00:39:31,869 --> 00:39:32,870
There you go.

573
00:39:33,829 --> 00:39:35,998
Things are tough for everybody these days.

574
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:38,751
It's not much, but when it comes to people
who care about you,

575
00:39:38,834 --> 00:39:42,505
you're richer than Elon Musk
and Lee Byung-chull combined.

576
00:39:42,588 --> 00:39:45,049
The higher-ups say
they'll cover your hospital bills.

577
00:39:45,132 --> 00:39:46,133
Stop eating.

578
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:48,052
But you still need a little something
in your wallet, you know?

579
00:39:48,135 --> 00:39:49,720
So you can stand up proud and tall.

580
00:39:50,679 --> 00:39:54,100
Hold your head high
while you're there, okay?

581
00:39:54,183 --> 00:39:58,145
We've done absolutely nothing wrong.

582
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:19,583
- Huh? Oh, hey, hey, hey, hey, don't…
- Wait, don't.

583
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:08,424
<i>We welcome our passengers aboard.</i>

584
00:41:08,507 --> 00:41:12,219
<i>Please be careful when moving around</i>
<i>while the train is in motion.</i>

585
00:41:16,724 --> 00:41:19,685
<i>Thank you for choosing</i>
<i>to ride with us today.</i>

586
00:41:20,686 --> 00:41:23,314
<i>We hope you have a pleasant journey.</i>

587
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:41,499
He'll be all right.

588
00:41:45,252 --> 00:41:47,213
Why did he have to
bow down like that, huh?

589
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:54,386
Why on earth would he bow down like that?

590
00:41:58,474 --> 00:41:59,850
He'll be all right.

591
00:42:02,269 --> 00:42:05,397
He has to be.

592
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:23,415
<i>We'd like to remind our passengers…</i>

593
00:42:23,499 --> 00:42:27,878
So we got to ride on the train,
meet you, take home some delicious food.

594
00:42:27,962 --> 00:42:30,297
It's been a really nice trip,
and we owe it all to you.

595
00:42:32,383 --> 00:42:34,260
I love taking the train, do you?

596
00:42:39,390 --> 00:42:40,683
Is this your first time on a train?

597
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:46,855
Oh, I see.

598
00:42:46,939 --> 00:42:51,819
So I guess you've never been anywhere else
other than Gwangju? Is that right?

599
00:42:55,614 --> 00:42:56,782
Why not?

600
00:43:13,257 --> 00:43:16,385
BECAUSE I FEEL GUILTY

601
00:43:27,187 --> 00:43:30,107
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

602
00:43:33,027 --> 00:43:35,904
1. CHIEF COMPLAINT: RECURRENT SEIZURES,
LEFT-SIDED FACIAL AND LIMB CLONIC MOVEMENT

603
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:38,824
2. PRESENT ILLNESS: INJURY FROM
BULLET FRAGMENT IN OCCIPITAL REGION

604
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:46,040
What on earth…

605
00:43:48,334 --> 00:43:50,002
really happened on that day?

606
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:02,681
Here you go. Enjoy.

607
00:44:03,307 --> 00:44:04,725
How do you like the food here?

608
00:44:10,147 --> 00:44:13,359
Uh, sir, did you sleep
comfortably last night?

609
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:16,195
Ah, good. I'm glad to hear it.

610
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:19,239
Wow, such nice weather today.

611
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,033
Oh, for sure. It's a beautiful day.

612
00:44:21,116 --> 00:44:22,785
Yeah, it's spring now.

613
00:44:22,868 --> 00:44:25,120
You should check out
the hospital's walking trail. It's great.

614
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,288
I'll take you there.

615
00:44:44,098 --> 00:44:48,519
Oh, wait. Uh…
We want you to make yourself at home.

616
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:51,855
While you're here, the hospital
will provide you with anything you need.

617
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:54,608
Um… Please don't feel bad
about accepting it.

618
00:44:56,652 --> 00:44:58,696
Ah! Thanks all for your hard work!

619
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:01,865
- Hello there!
- Hello, Mr. Oh Sang-beom!

620
00:45:01,949 --> 00:45:03,867
Wow, it's such a pleasure to meet you.

621
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:06,537
I'm Kim Chang-su,
the president of the SMA.

622
00:45:06,620 --> 00:45:08,455
I'm Mayor Im Ho-seok.

623
00:45:08,539 --> 00:45:11,125
Is there anything we can do
to make your stay more comfortable?

624
00:45:11,208 --> 00:45:15,045
I hope you'll be able to relax,
and get through your surgery safely,

625
00:45:15,129 --> 00:45:17,798
so you can heal from the injury and pain
you're experiencing.

626
00:45:17,881 --> 00:45:20,592
I'm so happy you're here, so happy. Here.

627
00:45:20,676 --> 00:45:23,303
You have such a friendly face.

628
00:45:23,387 --> 00:45:24,722
- Oh!
- Here…

629
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:27,099
That hurts! Ow!

630
00:45:27,182 --> 00:45:29,017
What the-- What do you think you're doing?

631
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:32,271
Since you're done shaking hands
with my patient, you can go now.

632
00:45:32,354 --> 00:45:35,649
- Huh?
- Hey, hold on. Do you know who this is?

633
00:45:35,733 --> 00:45:37,568
Dr. Gye, have you gone crazy?

634
00:45:38,277 --> 00:45:39,528
No, I haven't gone crazy.

635
00:45:39,611 --> 00:45:41,488
I've always been crazy.

636
00:45:41,572 --> 00:45:42,740
So you're Gye Su-jeong.

637
00:45:43,741 --> 00:45:45,117
- Mm-hmm.
- Really?

638
00:45:45,701 --> 00:45:48,704
You're exhausting my patient
with your tedious self-introductions,

639
00:45:48,787 --> 00:45:52,082
self-praise, long-winded speeches,
and grandstanding.

640
00:45:52,166 --> 00:45:54,918
So you better get lost.

641
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:57,713
"Get lost"?

642
00:45:57,796 --> 00:45:59,840
Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

643
00:45:59,923 --> 00:46:01,508
What's that? Is there a fire?

644
00:46:02,217 --> 00:46:03,552
- What?
- It's not a drill?

645
00:46:03,635 --> 00:46:06,054
- Is it a fire? What's going on?
- I think we should leave now.

646
00:46:06,138 --> 00:46:07,723
- Let's get you out of here.
- Where do I go?

647
00:46:07,806 --> 00:46:09,808
- Which way?
- Let's just get you to safety.

648
00:46:09,892 --> 00:46:11,852
- We need to go.
- Don't panic. Keep walking.

649
00:46:11,935 --> 00:46:13,520
Let's take the stairs to be safe.

650
00:46:27,534 --> 00:46:28,535
Dr. Gye.

651
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:33,791
I know you probably think
this is all pointless pretentiousness…

652
00:46:34,500 --> 00:46:37,920
and we're just a bunch of pathetic idiots.

653
00:46:39,630 --> 00:46:41,006
But the world we live in

654
00:46:41,089 --> 00:46:45,552
is not created and run by those
who keep saying "no" to life,

655
00:46:46,261 --> 00:46:49,181
but by the ones who keep saying "yes."

656
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:53,101
Director, let's get you out of here.

657
00:47:02,903 --> 00:47:03,904
Don't worry.

658
00:47:09,243 --> 00:47:10,953
Don't tell me… You didn't…

659
00:47:11,036 --> 00:47:12,830
I've always been tempted to press it.

660
00:47:13,580 --> 00:47:16,208
I just didn't think today
would turn out to be the day it happened.

661
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:19,211
So I reviewed the images we took.

662
00:47:20,504 --> 00:47:21,505
Mr. Oh Sang-beom…

663
00:47:23,298 --> 00:47:24,633
do you see visions of your brother?

664
00:47:30,430 --> 00:47:32,015
When I first met you,

665
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:34,351
you were sitting
on the very edge of the bench,

666
00:47:34,434 --> 00:47:36,061
<i>even though it was quite small.</i>

667
00:47:36,728 --> 00:47:39,273
And you were looking to the side.

668
00:47:40,357 --> 00:47:42,693
As if there was someone
sitting next to you on the bench.

669
00:47:42,776 --> 00:47:45,737
You were just looking at the old cemetery,
weren't you?

670
00:47:47,698 --> 00:47:48,907
Oh…

671
00:47:52,786 --> 00:47:54,413
He wasn't looking into the distance.

672
00:47:56,331 --> 00:47:59,418
<i>I heard you always carry a notepad</i>
<i>and a pencil around your neck.</i>

673
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:02,796
<i>But you didn't have them with you then.</i>

674
00:48:03,797 --> 00:48:05,591
<i>Because you didn't need them</i>
<i>to talk to him.</i>

675
00:48:09,469 --> 00:48:11,221
<i>And on the bench at the hospital,</i>

676
00:48:12,306 --> 00:48:13,724
<i>you were sitting the same way.</i>

677
00:48:15,058 --> 00:48:18,145
The surgery will help reduce
many symptoms:

678
00:48:18,228 --> 00:48:22,316
the tremors, the pain you feel,
the seizures,

679
00:48:22,399 --> 00:48:24,610
as well as the visual
and auditory hallucinations.

680
00:48:25,527 --> 00:48:28,155
So you probably wouldn't see
your brother again.

681
00:48:31,116 --> 00:48:33,827
I thought you should know that
before you decide.

682
00:48:52,429 --> 00:48:56,516
MY BROTHER IS A SYMPTOM?

683
00:48:57,517 --> 00:48:58,560
Yes.

684
00:49:07,653 --> 00:49:10,948
NOT A FIGMENT OF MY IMAGINATION?

685
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:13,784
You know the answer.

686
00:49:16,703 --> 00:49:17,746
Dr. Gye.

687
00:49:19,206 --> 00:49:21,833
Will you succeed… if you do the surgery?

688
00:49:24,002 --> 00:49:25,295
Yes, and…

689
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:29,716
it's because I never fail.

690
00:49:54,574 --> 00:49:57,828
I'M NOT DOING IT

691
00:50:34,239 --> 00:50:35,657
<i>I wish I could…</i>

692
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:38,326
<i>see him too.</i>

693
00:51:20,952 --> 00:51:22,871
I'M NOT DOING IT

694
00:51:34,591 --> 00:51:36,927
- What are you doing?
- Oh, you scared me.

695
00:51:38,095 --> 00:51:40,514
Do you have cat's paws for feet?
You're totally silent.

696
00:51:40,597 --> 00:51:42,724
He's sleeping, isn't he? Why are you here?

697
00:51:43,225 --> 00:51:44,226
Ah, yeah.

698
00:51:46,269 --> 00:51:47,437
Well, what are you doing here?

699
00:51:47,521 --> 00:51:50,690
Huh? Just dropping by on my way home.

700
00:51:50,774 --> 00:51:54,820
Oh! You leave work from the third floor
instead of the first?

701
00:51:55,695 --> 00:51:57,781
You're not as slow as you look, I guess.

702
00:51:59,825 --> 00:52:01,076
Ah, oh…

703
00:52:17,676 --> 00:52:20,262
Oh, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot.

704
00:52:20,345 --> 00:52:22,639
- Wow, it smells amazing.
- Right?

705
00:52:23,807 --> 00:52:25,016
- Here she is.
- I'm home everyone.

706
00:52:25,100 --> 00:52:27,185
- Oh, you're home.
- Hey! Sit down, come on.

707
00:52:27,269 --> 00:52:29,020
We forgot the sausages.

708
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:31,815
We have marinated crab and side dishes.
Sausages too?

709
00:52:31,898 --> 00:52:33,692
- Su-jeong likes them.
- <i>…being rushed to the hospital.</i>

710
00:52:33,775 --> 00:52:35,986
- It's a feast today, a feast.
- <i>We now turn to our reporter at the scene</i>

711
00:52:36,069 --> 00:52:37,445
- <i>for more details.</i>
- Wash your hands and come and sit.

712
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:40,282
Mr. Oh Sang-beom?

713
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:44,619
Mr. Oh Sang-beom. What?

714
00:52:56,590 --> 00:52:57,591
Oh, shit.

715
00:52:58,133 --> 00:53:00,302
- Still watching TV? What's so interesting?
<i>- At 7:50 p.m. today,</i>

716
00:53:00,385 --> 00:53:03,263
<i>Mr. Ji Du-seok, who served</i>
<i>as the country's 11th and 12th president,</i>

717
00:53:03,346 --> 00:53:06,308
<i>was found unconscious</i>
<i>in a sauna at a golf course</i>

718
00:53:06,391 --> 00:53:07,809
<i>in Gyeonggi-do.</i>

719
00:53:07,893 --> 00:53:12,105
<i>He was found in a state of cardiac arrest</i>
<i>and CPR was performed immediately.</i>

720
00:53:12,189 --> 00:53:14,900
<i>He is currently being transported</i>
<i>by helicopter to the Gyeonggi branch</i>

721
00:53:14,983 --> 00:53:17,569
<i>of Guseo University Medical Center.</i>

722
00:53:17,652 --> 00:53:20,113
<i>The exact cause of Mr. Ji's collapse</i>
<i>is still unknown…</i>

723
00:53:20,197 --> 00:53:21,198
PARK TAE-GYEONG

724
00:53:21,281 --> 00:53:24,075
Oh, Dr. Gye? Mr. Oh Sang-beom is gone.

725
00:53:24,159 --> 00:53:26,036
We've been looking for him.

726
00:53:26,119 --> 00:53:28,121
- But haven't found him yet.
- Damn it.

727
00:53:33,335 --> 00:53:35,545
<i>At that time, he was still unconscious</i>

728
00:53:35,629 --> 00:53:38,381
<i>and being supplied oxygen</i>
<i>through a respirator.</i>

729
00:53:38,465 --> 00:53:41,718
<i>Once again, to summarize</i>
<i>what we know so far:</i>

730
00:53:41,801 --> 00:53:46,556
<i>At around 7:50 p.m. this evening,</i>
<i>former President Ji Du-seok</i>

731
00:53:46,640 --> 00:53:48,058
<i>was found unconscious…</i>

732
00:53:48,141 --> 00:53:51,144
<i>…in a sauna at a golf course</i>
<i>in Gyeonggi-do.</i>

733
00:54:01,947 --> 00:54:04,407
Oh! Dr. Jo, it's him. See?

734
00:54:04,491 --> 00:54:07,035
But where-- where is that?

735
00:54:07,118 --> 00:54:08,536
It's the roof!

736
00:54:12,624 --> 00:54:14,209
Uh, he went up to the roof, Dr. Gye.

737
00:54:57,711 --> 00:54:59,629
Traffic's so bad.

738
00:55:01,756 --> 00:55:03,800
Huh?

739
00:55:04,592 --> 00:55:05,635
What's going on?

740
00:55:17,897 --> 00:55:19,274
Su-jeong.

741
00:55:19,357 --> 00:55:20,942
Su-jeong, hurry!

742
00:55:21,026 --> 00:55:23,903
Make sure you save him! No matter what!

743
00:56:22,212 --> 00:56:24,005
- Oh, Dr. Kim.
- Get in. Hurry up.

744
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:25,590
Is a helicopter here?

745
00:56:25,673 --> 00:56:26,925
It's on the way with Ji Du-seok on it.

746
00:57:07,549 --> 00:57:10,218
- No!
- Mr. Oh!

747
00:57:20,895 --> 00:57:22,772
No! Hold on tight!

748
00:57:24,858 --> 00:57:26,484
- Don't let him go!
- Snap out of it, please!

749
00:58:18,203 --> 00:58:20,788
No!

750
00:58:20,872 --> 00:58:23,082
Mr. Oh! Calm down!

751
00:58:36,179 --> 00:58:38,431
- No!
- Calm down!

752
00:58:39,140 --> 00:58:40,433
Please, Mr. Oh!

753
00:58:44,312 --> 00:58:45,939
Oh, please, please…

754
00:58:47,106 --> 00:58:48,650
Please!

755
00:58:53,988 --> 00:58:56,783
BECAUSE I FEEL GUILTY

756
00:59:01,996 --> 00:59:04,415
Gye Su-jeong, please help us.

757
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:17,845
Please…

758
00:59:17,929 --> 00:59:19,472
Oh, please…

759
00:59:19,556 --> 00:59:20,557
Oh, please…

760
00:59:21,641 --> 00:59:22,850
Please.

761
00:59:35,947 --> 00:59:38,825
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

762
00:59:38,908 --> 00:59:41,661
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

763
01:00:21,618 --> 01:00:23,703
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

764
01:00:23,786 --> 01:00:25,622
- Leave me alone!
- Mr. Oh, calm down. Do it, shoot it now!

765
01:00:25,705 --> 01:00:28,082
<i>Apparently,</i>
<i>they discussed transferring the patient</i>

766
01:00:28,166 --> 01:00:29,250
during the hospital meeting.

767
01:00:29,334 --> 01:00:30,376
<i>So the hospital is giving up on him?</i>

768
01:00:30,460 --> 01:00:32,003
<i>He's asking to be discharged.</i>

769
01:00:32,086 --> 01:00:35,381
You need to live! You need to try living!

770
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:37,675
<i>What do you mean,</i>
<i>Mr. Oh Sang-beom is missing?</i>

771
01:00:37,759 --> 01:00:39,218
Get in! Quickly!

772
01:00:39,302 --> 01:00:42,263
<i>You know, don't you, Dr. Gye?</i>
<i>There's a way, right?</i>

773
01:00:42,347 --> 01:00:45,016
Think. I need to think. I need to find it.

774
01:00:45,099 --> 01:00:48,936
<i>Everyone will soon find out</i>
<i>about the lie you told, Dr. Gye.</i>
